Local patch, not from upstream. Written against FrankenPHP v1.12.7 / main, which were the
same commit at the time (github.com/php/frankenphp).

php-src commit e0221be8 (2026-07-30, master/8.6.0-dev) changed PG(output_handler) from
char * to zend_string *, so FrankenPHP's char * usage stops compiling against php-src
master. Upstream had not adapted as of v1.12.7. The 8.6 branch mirrors what php-src's own
main.c does at request startup, including dropping the empty-string check: output_handler
is registered with OnUpdateStrNotEmpty, which rejects empty values, so a non-NULL
zero-length handler cannot occur. The PHP_VERSION_ID split keeps the 8.5 build byte-identical
to unpatched upstream.

The apply step in php/franken{,-testing}/Dockerfile detects when upstream adopts the
zend_string * API and skips this patch, so the build picks the fix up on its own. Delete
this file and that block once the skip branch is what fires.

--- a/frankenphp.c
+++ b/frankenphp.c
@@ -586,10 +586,17 @@
                       sizeof(SAPI_PHP_VERSION_HEADER) - 1, 1);
     }
 
+#if PHP_VERSION_ID >= 80600
+    if (PG(output_handler)) {
+      zval oh;
+
+      ZVAL_STR(&oh, zend_string_dup(PG(output_handler), 0));
+#else
     if (PG(output_handler) && PG(output_handler)[0]) {
       zval oh;
 
       ZVAL_STRING(&oh, PG(output_handler));
+#endif
       php_output_start_user(&oh, 0, PHP_OUTPUT_HANDLER_STDFLAGS);
       zval_ptr_dtor(&oh);
     } else if (PG(output_buffering)) {
